# Unsealing dep's sealed interface S changes no member, only drops its PermittedSubclasses
# attribute. It still changes what compiles against S: an exhaustive
# `switch (s) { case X x -> ...; case Y y -> ...; }` stops compiling. So the change must reach S's
# API hash, or dependents of S are not recompiled.
# `use` only refers to S, in Java 17 syntax, because pattern matching in switch needs Java 21 and
# this test runs on JDK 17 too. For a Java dependent, being recompiled is the whole question.
> use/compile
$ sleep 2000
$ copy-file changes/S.java dep/src/main/java/S.java
> use/checkRecompilations 1 A
